' diagram-type: state-machine
@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title v0002 State Registry - Executor Capacity State Machine

note as ConcreteNaming
  Concrete Executor services follow the platform naming convention
  documented in AGENTS.md:
    executor_<runtime>_<tool>
  Current concrete Executor: executor_docker_opehands
  (runtime = docker, tool = openhands; "opehands" is the service
  identifier; the external product spelling "OpenHands" stays
  unchanged). The state machine below is generic over every concrete
  Executor under the executor_<runtime>_<tool> family.
end note

state "Executor local: available" as ExAvail
state "Executor local: full" as ExFull

[*] --> ExAvail : Executor starts\nscope + tag immutable\nlocally observes max_capacity, running_count

ExAvail --> ExFull : Executor local\nrunning_count >= max_capacity
ExFull --> ExAvail : Executor local\nlocal runtime terminates

note right of ExAvail
  When available, Executor discovers
  pending tasks matching eligibility
  and tag, ordered (ingested_at ASC,
  task_id ASC), then claims oldest
  eligible pending with command_id.
  Only starts runtime after 200 claimed.
end note

note right of ExFull
  When full, Executor stops discovery
  and claim requests. Registry emits
  no capacity-based rejection
  (no 422 executor_at_capacity).
end note

note as TeamInvariant
  scope = team: Executor bound to one
  immutable team_id referencing existing
  team; envelope team_id verified against
  authenticated Executor; foreign
  identifiers -> non-revealing 404.
  scope = system: no team binding;
  envelope team_id verified against
  parent task team_id; same-team
  requirement becomes parent-task
  team_id verification only.
end note

note as Observations
  Executor appends executor_events with
  executor_id NOT NULL; envelope team_id
  matches scope. Latest max_capacity and
  running_count mirror onto executors
  in the same transaction. Observations
  never gate discovery, claim, or events.
end note

note as RegistryContract
  Claim responses:
  - 200 claimed
  - 409 older_task_must_be_claimed_first
  - 409 task_already_claimed
  - same (task_id, command_id) retry is
    idempotent 200 claimed
  - non-revealing 404 for unknown/foreign
  No 422 executor_at_capacity.
end note

note as ImageSource
  resolved_image set atomically at the
  Created transition from four-level
  precedence. Executor uses it verbatim
  and refuses the task if it cannot be
  pulled or started. No local image
  fallback; no substitution.
end note

note as Scope
  scope = team: flowai.team_id = auth team,
  flowai.executor_scope = team,
  flowai.command_id = claim command_id.
  scope = system: flowai.team_id = parent
  task team_id, flowai.executor_scope = system,
  flowai.command_id = claim command_id.
end note

@enduml